@node compressor Plugin Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

Standard feedforward dynamics processor. Detector path: optional Butterworth high-pass on the sidechain, peak or RMS level detection, attack/release smoothing. Gain computer applies the ratio above the (soft-knee) threshold. Output stage applies make-up gain and optional dry/wet mix for parallel compression. Look-ahead inserts a delay line on the audio path so the detector sees the future of the signal.

@subsubheading Parameter wiring

All parameters reach the audio thread through the host's @code{rebuild_cached_parameters} / @code{set_parameter} / @code{get_parameter} triad. Structural parameters (marked in the notes below) trigger a rebuild; the rest update in real time with zero dropouts.

@subsubheading Source

The @code{compressor} plugin does not have a dedicated crate at the time of writing; its implementation lives under @file{crates/sotf-plugins/crates/sotf-host/} or one of the multi-component crates. Search the workspace for the plugin type key @code{"compressor"} to locate it.

Run the unit tests with @code{cargo test -p sotf-plugin-compressor}.

